{
 "about": {
  "what": "Berth points ESTIMATED from EarthAtlas's own AIS positions (Josh 2026-09-28), for terminals with several berths but only one citable position. Never an official position: stored as terminal_berths basis 'ais_inferred' (source 'earthatlas-ais-berths', evidence class inferred) and labelled \"estimated from AIS stops\" on the card.",
  "method": "scripts/ships/bake-ais/berth_stops.py: long stops of large ships (MarineCadastre AIS, CC0; SOG < 0.5 kn for 2 h+, length >= 100 m as broadcast; position = median, spread = 90th percentile). scripts/ships/ais-berths.mjs + lib/ships/aisBerths.js: stops that spread <= 50 m are clustered (densest stop seeds a cluster of the stops within 60 m of its median); a cluster becomes a berth of terminal T only if it passes the footprint guard.",
  "guard": "1) the cluster centre lies inside T's own mapped footprint (the OpenStreetMap site / pier elements listed under footprints) or within 80 m of it (a moored ship's AIS position lies alongside the quay); 2) no other terminal's footprint and no other named mapped facility (OSM industrial site or pier) is within 80 m or closer than 2x T's distance (else ambiguous, not attributed); 3) >= 80% of its stops are by ships whose AIS type fits T (70-79 cargo at dry bulk / grain; 80-89 tanker where T handles liquids); 4) >= 10 stops by >= 5 different ships; 5) outside every existing official / OSM berth radius of T (inside one, those ships are already counted).",
  "positions": "lat/lon = the cluster centre (median of the stop positions), from AIS (CC0). The OSM footprint only decides WHICH terminal a cluster belongs to; no OSM coordinate is copied into a berth position.",
  "official_lists": "Official berth facts (names, lengths, depths) from the Pacific Pilotage Authority's berth parameters and the port authority's soundings sheets are recorded in salish-terminals.json official_berths (Josh 2026-09-29: facts are not copyrightable), each cited to its document; Richardson ais-1 and Vancouver Wharves ais-1 are paired with official berths there. Nothing from those documents is stored in this file.",
  "proposal": "scripts/ships/ais-berths.mjs run 2026-09-29 UTC (stops 2025-07-01 … 2026-06-30, 365 days; OSM base 2026-09-29T03:17:16Z): 3 accepted, 23 rejected; reviewed by hand 2026-09-28."
 },
